WEBVTT

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.470
<i>A news flash has arrived</i> <i>from our Dakar press center.</i>

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:55.900
Here they come!

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.650
<i>Fusion reactor shutdown confirmed.</i> <i>No chain reaction.</i>

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.110
<i>Intense heat source detected...</i> <i>Incoming!</i>

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.640
<i>You're taking too long to launch!</i> <i>What's the holdup?!</i>

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.310
<i>I need a sit-rep!</i>

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:12.110
I still can't believe they're attacking the capital.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.960
I've been waiting for this moment!

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:45.850
Father, Mother... It's all the Federation's fault!

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.810
<i>Loni, enemy reinforcements are coming.</i>

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:51.190
<i>We've done enough!</i> <i>The diversion worked.</i>

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.730
<i>Now we wait to hear from</i> <i>the Garencieres Team.</i>

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.820
Roger.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.950
So, it has begun... We must resolve this swiftly.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:12.210
Indeed... However, the key to Laplace's Box, the Unicorn,

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:17.300
vanished in the battle that destroyed the old prime minister's residence.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.090
And remains missing.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.090
Nevertheless, if Master Cardeas saw fit to choose him...

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.270
God is toying with us...

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:35.900
Or rather, has Cardeas' "mankind's" dream been fulfilled?

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.410
Banagher, my flesh and blood...

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.750
<b>At the Bottom of the Gravity Well</b>

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:56.090
<i>Zeon remnants have remained dormant in</i> <i>the three years since Char's Rebellion.</i>

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.760
<i>Does this sudden act of terrorism</i> <i>signal a new uprising by them?</i>

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.970
<i>Some pundits believe this to be</i> <i>the opening salvo of a third-</i>

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:09.510
Damn it all... Why is he summoning me out to his home at a time like this?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.850
I protest the implication.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.940
Unlike the attack on Lhasa three years ago,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:23.110
this one on Dakar cost the lives of many government workers, as well.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.490
I must say, this mutual mudslinging is most unproductive.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:33.210
I would prefer to have a more constructive discussion, Ms. Martha.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.620
I'll cut to the chase, then.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.790
Please hand over the VIP that is currently in your care.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.550
What are you talking about?

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.760
It is in the best interests of both our sides, as well as yours personally,

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.720
Chairman Ronan Marcenas.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.730
<i>Leaving aside my interests for the</i> <i>moment, what do you stand to gain?</i>

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.810
I'll leave that to your imagination. Deliver her to-

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.570
Please contact me again in two hours' time.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.690
I have an urgent matter to solve.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.650
As you wish.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.660
I'm dying to ask the Chairman,

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.910
what "urgent matter" could be more important than the Zabi orphan?

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.600
I know what a difficult situation this puts you in. But she-

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.680
You've fallen for her, haven't you?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.810
That's why you deserted and fled here.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.400
It's just like when you ran away from home, saying you wanted to be a pilot.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.320
I didn't expect you to get yourself mixed up with the Box...

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.450
You need to learn the truth behind the Marcenas family.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:55.370
Given the situation, that is the only way that you will survive this.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.670
Grant us your salvation.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.170
Salvation...

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.220
<i>At present, the military and the fire department</i>

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.350
<i>are doing everything they can to locate survivors.</i>

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.560
<i>What should I do? Banagher...{i0\i0}</i>

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.190
What nerve!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.900
Riddhe?

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.330
Forgive me.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.620
What is the matter?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.870
I've learned that I come from a shameful family.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.460
Shameful?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:45.800
My family, the Marcenas family, acts as a mirror image of the Vist Foundation.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.630
That is how we have managed to survive through the Universal Century.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:55.060
I know my family will stop at nothing to prevent the release of Laplace's Box.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.640
Even using you as a hostage again.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.650
The only way to prevent that is to get the Box

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.270
before either the Foundation or the Neo Zeon.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.110
Either that, or destroy-

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.400
Its key? The Unicorn?

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:17.580
I've brought you to the worst possible place.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.120
And here I thought I could help you...

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.920
Come what may, I'll protect you.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.130
So please, stay here. By my side...

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:31.300
Don't leave me alone.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.730
<i>Will... Will you become a member of my family?</i>

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:45.770
<i>Leave Zeon and the Zabi family</i> <i>and join the Marcenas family.</i>

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:49.940
<i>If you did that, even father would have to...</i> <i>Even if it's just for show.</i>

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:55.450
<i>You could put an end to this pointless</i> <i>fighting and win your freedom.</i>

00:07:55.450 --> 00:08:00.660
<i>That kind of freedom... Would you</i> <i>really call that being free?</i>

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.420
Everything is clear.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.850
Ple Twelve.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.060
That's your name, isn't it? Answer me.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.730
You're to obey your master's orders.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.060
You aren't my master.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:31.230
If you want to make me obey, you'll have to try reconditioning or torturing me.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.150
M-Mind your tone!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.910
We've learned that reconditioning you would be difficult.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.700
You were made too well.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.790
Still, that is for the best.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.790
I have no interest in a doll whose memories can simply be swapped out.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.130
What I truly want is...

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.640
The Mass Production Type Qubeley. The machine you all used to pilot.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.060
Artificially-created Newtypes.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:05.350
Puppets that do the bidding of their master.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:11.360
Your soul is still held prisoner within that machine.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.820
You were created as a tool of war by men who knew nothing but spilling blood.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.910
Considering that true life is born from a woman's womb,

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.080
don't you find that unnatural?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.700
I am going to free you from that machine.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:42.180
This is a camouflaged Sleeves freighter that made Earthfall some ten days ago.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.350
I've heard about the ruins of Laplace being destroyed.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.310
Are you saying that these people were responsible?

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.400
I want you to use your ship to locate them.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:56.400
In short, you wish to use the Ra Cailum for personal reasons?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.400
This ship was also involved in the incidents at Industrial 7 and Palau.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.000
As commander of the Londo Bell, aren't you also concerned

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.040
about the safety of the Nahel Argama?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:10.460
At present, she is being detained in Earth orbit.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:14.880
The order came from the Vist Foundation via General Staff HQ.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.630
I don't want to be seen as taking hostages,

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.760
so I've laid my cards on the table first.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.520
The Foundation is after this ship, as well.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.690
If we take it into custody first, it will give us the upper hand.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.520
What is so special about this ship?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:34.860
This ship is carrying something called Laplace's Box.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:39.820
In the event you are unable to capture it, I want you to destroy it.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.990
You give me too much credit, sir.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:46.790
I've simply had a career slightly outside the norm, I'm not-

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:51.500
Captain a series of motherships for Gundam types since the One Year War,

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.900
and you will naturally be seen as a commander of a Newtype corps.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.340
That does seem to be my luck, sir.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:04.100
An example of being taken advantage of if you display your talents too overtly.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:06.260
There is one other favor I want to ask of you.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.690
I have an unworthy son who serves as a military pilot.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.060
I would like you to take him aboard your-

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:13.810
What is it?

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.480
Begging your pardon, sir.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:20.450
What is it, Doillon? I told you I wasn't to be disturbed until...

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:26.910
The Lady Mineva has disappeared from her room.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.120
We are searching the vicinity as we speak.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.110
Sorry, I'm the last person you want advice from on this,

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:59.150
but the only way to get the mobile suits out is to crack the hull.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:04.860
We'll save that as a last resort. That would wreck the Garencieres.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:09.830
Sir, if we don't link up with friendly forces soon, the enemy will find us.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.170
Even if they do say their diversion worked.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:16.250
I still can't believe they hit Dakar, of all places.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.920
I can understand how they feel.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:23.840
After all, the people waiting on Earth missed out on two Neo Zeon wars.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:30.640
There's no telling what stunt they'll pull next if we don't make contact.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.100
There's an oasis about 60km east of here.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:38.980
Let's make a quick trip there by mobile suit, then make contact with our allies.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.360
At this point, wrecking the ship is-

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.610
Rushing is pointless, and this won't work if the Unicorn isn't operational.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:48.870
We could always tie up the kid inside the cockpit and bring the whole suit.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.040
The next set of coordinates the La+ program gave

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.040
are in one seriously inconvenient place.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.960
Give me the map.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.130
Damn it, what is he thinking?

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:04.590
Why the hell would he bring you, of all people?

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.180
Bastard!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.850
Don't think we won't kill you just because you're the Unicorn's pilot!

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.810
I'm not thinking that at-

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:22.320
I know that this is all my fault. I killed Mr. Gilboa.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.860
You bet your ass it is!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.240
He could've put us down safe and sound,

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:31.200
even with your Unicorn latched onto the ship during atmospheric entry like that.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.470
On the house. Drink up.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.390
I like the way you dig in.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.470
It's nice to see a young lady who isn't obsessed with good manners.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:58.060
Thank you, I will.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:01.810
I haven't seen you around before. Whereabouts do you hail from?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:09.740
A Spacenoid, huh? Certainly explains why I haven't seen you before.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:18.000
You sightseeing? There isn't much around here to see.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.880
Not at all. As someone born and raised in space,

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.960
I'm happy to be able to set foot on the ground.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.840
To people like me, there are times when gravity isn't kind.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:33.390
Makes me wonder if my back wouldn't bother me anymore if I went into space.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:36.180
You have lived on Earth your entire life?

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:39.390
Yeah. I'm too old to leave her now.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:49.280
My generation was raised on stories of the bad old days

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.990
from our grandfathers and grandmothers.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.490
Sounds like things got pretty terrible back then.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.420
They wanted to do something about it,

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:04.790
so they founded the Federation and got the space settlement thing started.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:16.890
Some folks say it was only the poor that were forcibly discarded into space,

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.270
but there were a lot of people who left of their own accord.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:25.610
They were prepared to stay away until the Earth's environment recovered.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:30.860
But then the One Year War undid most of the progress that had been made.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.570
We're hopeless, aren't we?

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:41.160
Well, what can you do? It all began out of good intentions.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.120
Good intentions?

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:48.210
Both the Federation and the space settlement began with the hope of saving humanity.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:53.130
Like wanting your business to succeed, or making a better life for your family.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:57.310
But that can turn into something better described as egotism.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.810
Maybe so.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.730
But if we denied that, this would be a sad world.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:08.610
I guess there are some who can work for the greater good at their own expense,

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.400
but there's something shady about it.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.610
Like that Char guy with the Neo Zeon.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.780
He said he was fighting for the good of everyone,

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.330
even while he was dropping asteroids on us.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:23.500
Truth is, maybe he was just a guy who never learned to love humanity.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.750
What can we do, then?

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:29.380
Hell if I know. We never figured that out.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:34.260
I think we tried, but in the end, we just postponed paying our debts,

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:38.140
and I spent my life regretting not being able to do anything for you people.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:42.390
All I can do is just make you a cup of coffee.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.070
I see... I suppose you're right.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.040
What can I possibly do?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.380
The coffee was delicious.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:11.500
This alone made my coming to Earth worthwhile.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:19.050
Miss Audrey Burne. Chairman Ronan is waiting.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.470
Come with us, please.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.010
You're...

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:27.850
I am Mineva Zabi. I have no intention of running or hiding.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:29.520
Stand aside.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.090
I'm having Mineva Zabi brought here.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.720
I plan to use her as bait to recapture the Unicorn.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.550
She will probably obey, too.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:17:59.680
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.350
You can be the one to give her the orders.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.270
U-Understood.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.920
<i>Why me?</i>

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.840
<i>Because you look like you have</i> <i>the most time on your hands.</i>

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.760
<i>It's impossible. You can't walk four days through a desert.</i>

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.840
<i>There's a way to do it.</i>

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.460
Idiot.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:55.510
Didn't I tell you to take regular sips even if you're not thirsty?

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.610
Please, just leave me here.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.820
Do you want me to tell you to hang in there or something?

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.700
Please, leave me alone. I'm sick of it.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.500
Of being caught up in things I don't understand, and being used.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:11.920
Sorry, I can't do that. You're a pilot.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:15.130
Get out of the victim mindset and quit sulking.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.820
Gilboa would roll over in his grave.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.740
I didn't mean to kill him!

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:23.930
Mr. Daguza died, and my head went completely blank.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.370
If you can't forgive me, just get it over with!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:27.100
That's not true.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.310
Your eyes say that you don't believe that for one minute.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.820
Those are the eyes of a man who decides for himself how he lives and dies.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.570
So until you do die, put on a brave face for others to see.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.610
A man's life is a struggle until the day he dies.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.440
<i>...try with all your might,</i> <i>the path will show itself to you!</i>

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:52.120
<i>You go fulfill your own role.</i>

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.280
I did... That's what I did! For all I was worth!

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.300
And look at what happened!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:04.970
I fought and killed in a mobile suit, and now I'm walking across a desert!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:10.890
What more am I supposed to do?! What do you want me to fight?!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:56.310
<i>We were prisoners of war here in Africa.</i>

00:20:56.310 --> 00:21:02.260
<i>In the camp, the Treaty didn't</i> <i>count for anything, but that's okay.</i>

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.010
<i>Zeons are Zeons.</i>

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:08.140
<i>To the Feds, we were the devils</i> <i>who'd dropped a colony.</i>

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:11.650
<i>While the bigwigs were negotiating a peace,</i>

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:17.080
<i>the Fed troops sent to occupy our</i> <i>homeland were getting frustrated.</i>

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.790
<i>They'd been brought up on stuff like,</i>

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:24.280
<i>"Kill the demonic Zeon!" and "If you</i> <i>want a woman, get one in Zeon!"</i>

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:28.180
<i>They needed a scapegoat to appease them.</i>

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:34.810
<i>And then one night, a town was overrun</i> <i>by soldiers who came out of nowhere.</i>

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.230
<i>The elderly, begging for their lives,</i> <i>children clinging to their mothers,</i>

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.560
<i>they killed every last person.</i>

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:46.030
<i>Officially, it was written off as</i> <i>troops pacifying rioting citizens,</i>

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:50.030
<i>but it was obvious to everyone</i> <i>that they were blowing off steam.</i>

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:53.270
<i>That town's name was Globe.</i>

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:57.980
<i>My mom and dad lived there.</i> <i>So did the Captain's family.</i>

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:03.130
<i>His wife and their daughter, who'd just turned five...</i>

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:21.060
<i>The revival of Zeon wouldn't</i> <i>bring any of them back,</i>

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:23.970
<i>and I don't give a rat's ass</i> <i>what's inside that box.</i>

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:27.430
<i>But do we die in vain, cursing the world?</i>

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:29.990
<i>Or do we keep fighting an endless war?</i>

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:33.940
<i>Those were our two choices.</i>

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:40.150
Why are you crying?

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:42.420
It's so beautiful.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:47.990
It almost makes you doubt all those stories about the Earth being polluted.

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:51.590
Thing is, the air around here is even more polluted than it used to be.

00:22:51.590 --> 00:22:55.970
And they say the desert has advanced all the way to Dakar's doorstep.

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:59.390
It's all humanity's doing.

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:03.090
Indiscriminate development, the dropped colonies and asteroid...

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:05.630
If humanity is the product of nature,

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:10.070
that makes all of mankind's trash and poison natural products, too.

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:12.850
And even if it's rendered unfit for human habitation,

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:17.450
I guess that'll be the result of nature achieving a new balance.

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:20.570
Mother nature has absolutely no mercy.

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:23.500
Ancient humans understood that.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:27.420
As products of nature, they knew it instinctively.

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:33.250
So to survive, they protected themselves by creating civilization and societies.

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:37.080
Yeah. But they got too complicated, and before they knew it,

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:41.940
people were forced to live for the purpose of maintaining the system.

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:45.970
In the end, it made life hard to live.

00:23:45.970 --> 00:23:51.180
And to escape that topsy-turvy world, they went into space to find new lands.

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:54.680
There, they created a different system.

00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:58.690
A natural development that gave hope and direction

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:01.520
to those cast out into space, the Spacenoids.

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.650
That was Zeon.

00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:07.610
The old system left behind on Earth rejected it.

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:12.200
Because systems from two different birthplaces are never compatible.

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:16.000
It always ends with one of them trying to force the other into submission.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:19.120
But in the past, a world with a unified government like the Federation

00:24:19.120 --> 00:24:21.960
and ten billion people living in space

00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:24.690
must have sounded like a fairy tale.

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:28.300
Doesn't humanity have the possibility to do it?

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:31.550
To make two ways of thinking merge into one someday?

00:24:31.550 --> 00:24:34.720
We all aren't governed fairly and equally.

00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:40.690
The hatred of the beaten and downtrodden clings to the Earth to this day.

00:24:41.230 --> 00:24:43.580
That's a sad thing.

00:24:45.730 --> 00:24:48.630
Yeah... I suppose it is.

00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:52.990
Even though we live our lives trying to escape sadness...

00:24:52.990 --> 00:24:54.260
I wonder why that is?

00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:07.760
Banagher.

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:12.390
I know, I know. A man doesn't cry in front of other people, right?

00:25:12.390 --> 00:25:13.590
No.

00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:18.270
Crying because you care is a different matter.

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:24.250
I don't trust people who never cry, no matter what.

00:25:49.610 --> 00:25:51.260
Banagher.

00:25:53.430 --> 00:25:55.280
I owe you.

00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:58.820
If it weren't for you, I might've given up along the way, too.

00:25:58.820 --> 00:26:02.160
Don't thank me, all I did was slow you down.

00:26:02.160 --> 00:26:06.160
Having someone to butt heads with can make all the difference.

00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:09.670
Does the Garencieres Team have a new member?

00:26:09.670 --> 00:26:12.400
That's a bad habit, Captain.

00:26:13.950 --> 00:26:16.240
Okay, stop right there!

00:26:16.240 --> 00:26:18.680
Good work.

00:26:19.490 --> 00:26:20.950
Captain.

00:26:21.550 --> 00:26:28.020
Someone once told me to think of a better way to use the Box.

00:26:28.020 --> 00:26:30.940
What if that's my...

00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:35.650
Where is it? Where is the Unicorn's next set of coordinates?

00:26:36.240 --> 00:26:38.280
<i>It's Torrington this time, eh?</i>

00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:41.780
<i>This Box certainly keeps giving us</i> <i>one difficult location after the other.</i>

00:26:42.180 --> 00:26:47.330
<i>It makes me wonder if we're being</i> <i>played for fools by Cardeas Vist.</i>

00:26:47.330 --> 00:26:50.900
<i>Nicely done at Dakar, Lt. Commander Kirks.</i>

00:26:50.900 --> 00:26:55.160
<i>Thanks to your distracting them</i> <i>with your Earth Zeon Remnants,</i>

00:26:55.160 --> 00:26:57.530
<i>we were able to protect the Garencieres.</i>

00:26:57.530 --> 00:26:58.760
<i>You have my gratitude.</i>

00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:04.290
And you ours, sir. The Zee Zulus proved to be formidable assets.

00:27:04.290 --> 00:27:09.850
<i>Ah, you must be Ensign Loni Garvey.</i> <i>I am familiar with your father.</i>

00:27:09.850 --> 00:27:13.670
<i>He has done us a great service,</i> <i>perfecting Haman's legacy as he did.</i>

00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:17.280
Captain, my life's sole purpose is to settle the scores that haunt the souls

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:20.060
of my father and mother, and their comrades.

00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:20.700
Loni!

00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:25.160
I would like you to assign us the mission to attack Torrington.

00:27:25.830 --> 00:27:28.190
If we unload the Split-horn Gundam there,

00:27:28.190 --> 00:27:31.000
we should learn the whereabouts of Laplace's Box.

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:37.700
<i>I lead the Neo Zeon who have made</i> <i>their stronghold in space.</i>

00:27:37.700 --> 00:27:40.490
<i>I have no right to issue orders</i> <i>to you and your forces,</i>

00:27:40.490 --> 00:27:44.510
<i>who have been waging a guerilla war</i> <i>on Earth since the One Year War.</i>

00:27:44.510 --> 00:27:48.600
In that case, may I take that to mean that you also have no right to stop us?

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:52.270
<i>May the heavens protect the heir to Mahdi's cause.</i>

00:27:52.880 --> 00:27:54.380
Sieg Zeon!

00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:08.910
Captain, is this wise? Dakar was bad enough, but this will-

00:28:08.910 --> 00:28:11.610
<i>I understand your misgivings, Captain.</i>

00:28:11.620 --> 00:28:14.580
<i>Nevertheless, they have been waiting all this time.</i>

00:28:14.580 --> 00:28:16.750
<i>Waiting while time stood still around them.</i>

00:28:17.110 --> 00:28:19.800
<i>People grow accustomed to waiting.</i>

00:28:19.800 --> 00:28:22.870
<i>I expect that they could have</i> <i>gone on waiting forever.</i>

00:28:22.870 --> 00:28:28.140
<i>However, time has begun to flow again.</i> <i>Because of Cardeas Vist's actions.</i>

00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:32.600
<i>If we do nothing, the waters will</i> <i>only become hopelessly muddied.</i>

00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:35.710
<i>Do you not agree, Captain?</i>

00:28:35.710 --> 00:28:41.110
<i>To prevent that, I have another job</i> <i>for the Garencieres.</i>

00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:43.500
Here you go.

00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:44.860
Sure thing.

00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:49.120
So, you're the pilot of the Split-horn.

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:51.100
The key to the Box.

00:28:51.100 --> 00:28:51.860
Key?

00:28:51.860 --> 00:28:53.040
I expect great things from you.

00:28:58.210 --> 00:29:02.010
They say she was piloting the behemoth at Dakar.

00:29:02.010 --> 00:29:04.170
A girl like her?

00:29:13.520 --> 00:29:15.270
Message from Kirks Team!

00:29:15.270 --> 00:29:17.340
The ones who attacked Dakar, huh?

00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:20.720
This is a code used by the old Principality.

00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:22.840
It's a watchword dating back to the Third Landing Operation,

00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:26.410
when our first forces came down to Earth during the One Year War.

00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:28.020
What does it say?

00:29:28.020 --> 00:29:33.100
"About to give the Feds the shock of their lives! Request assistance!

00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:35.190
Dakar was only the beginning!"

00:30:31.710 --> 00:30:33.920
Dolphin 02, signal lost!

00:30:33.920 --> 00:30:35.250
Damage report!

00:30:35.250 --> 00:30:37.420
Sonar, waiting for explosion sounds to die down.

00:30:37.420 --> 00:30:39.130
Aquatic ordnance, all green.

00:30:39.130 --> 00:30:40.770
Propulsion, values nominal!

00:30:40.770 --> 00:30:44.730
Dolphin 01, still engaging two unknown mobile suits!

00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:47.280
Can we launch our reserve suits?!

00:30:47.280 --> 00:30:49.490
Three minutes until flooding is complete!

00:31:10.330 --> 00:31:12.950
They say we're to drop this off at the coordinate point

00:31:12.950 --> 00:31:16.220
once the base is captured, then wait for new info to be revealed.

00:31:16.880 --> 00:31:19.770
They say Ivan's gonna be our escort.

00:31:20.810 --> 00:31:22.460
What's wrong, Banagher?

00:31:22.460 --> 00:31:27.890
It's strange. You know, for Zeon weapons to fit a Federation mobile suit.

00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:32.560
That's 'cause both sides use a universal standard.

00:31:32.560 --> 00:31:36.870
If their parts can get along, why can't they quit fighting?

00:31:36.870 --> 00:31:41.190
That's the one thing that mellowed out while they were fighting.

00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:42.960
It was more efficient that way.

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:45.960
You mean it worked better for Anaheim Electronics?

00:31:45.960 --> 00:31:51.260
And it worked better in the field, too. It's helping us right now, right?

00:31:59.670 --> 00:32:00.850
That's it, huh?

00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:12.700
He's good.

00:32:13.770 --> 00:32:16.200
We are on a course for New Guinea.

00:32:16.600 --> 00:32:21.730
The Federation Forces submarine Bonefish has gone missing in the Coral Sea.

00:32:21.730 --> 00:32:25.500
Given the state of the scene, there is a strong possibility that she was sunk.

00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:28.400
If this is related to the camouflaged ship we are hunting,

00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:31.130
we may encounter and engage the enemy with no warning.

00:32:31.130 --> 00:32:36.470
Our top priority is to secure Laplace's Box, but we may not have that luxury.

00:32:36.790 --> 00:32:38.540
Stay sharp while you are out there.

00:32:38.540 --> 00:32:39.680
Yes, sir!

00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:42.700
Captain Bright.

00:32:42.700 --> 00:32:43.520
What is it?

00:32:44.210 --> 00:32:48.930
I'd appreciate it if you would stop giving me special treatment.

00:32:48.930 --> 00:32:53.300
Whatever my background, I am an E.F.S.F. pilot.

00:32:53.300 --> 00:32:55.490
Please don't take me off dangerous missions to-

00:32:55.490 --> 00:32:57.410
Get over yourself!

00:32:57.410 --> 00:33:02.730
Thinking that way proves that you are giving yourself special treatment.

00:33:02.730 --> 00:33:07.030
I never had any intention of doing so, no matter who you are.

00:33:07.030 --> 00:33:09.040
If I need you, I will use you.

00:33:09.040 --> 00:33:12.910
However, if you launch, make sure that you come back alive.

00:33:12.910 --> 00:33:16.800
If you can do that, I'll see you as a pilot like any other.

00:33:16.800 --> 00:33:18.180
Yes, sir.

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:22.310
It's me. Put it through.

00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:23.850
It's Bright.

00:33:29.260 --> 00:33:31.260
What did you say?!

00:33:33.400 --> 00:33:35.400
Why do you suppose it's that place?

00:33:35.930 --> 00:33:38.350
It's where the colony was dropped.

00:33:38.350 --> 00:33:40.440
Damn that Cardeas Vist...

00:33:40.440 --> 00:33:45.110
Is he trying to make us retrace the path of humanity's downfall or something?

00:33:45.110 --> 00:33:47.580
That kid will be fine.

00:33:47.980 --> 00:33:51.950
Still, if he defied us for real in that suit, we couldn't do a thing to stop him.

00:33:51.950 --> 00:33:55.590
Right now, he has total faith in you, Captain.

00:33:58.830 --> 00:34:00.600
<i>Ms. Loni...</i>

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:26.330
<i>Massive mobile armor approaching from shore!</i>

00:35:26.330 --> 00:35:28.890
<i>Torrington Base, requesting assistance!</i>

00:36:02.220 --> 00:36:05.220
Russet, Candor! Scatter! The next wave is coming!

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:07.390
Loni! Avoid the city!

00:36:07.390 --> 00:36:09.500
There's no need to take a detour.

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:11.750
Have you forgotten what the Federation did to us?

00:36:11.750 --> 00:36:14.550
<i>It'll create unnecessary casualties. Keep your cool!</i>

00:36:14.550 --> 00:36:15.650
Acknowledged...

00:36:16.260 --> 00:36:16.860
What?!

00:36:17.590 --> 00:36:19.190
<i>What's the matter, Loni?</i>

00:36:19.720 --> 00:36:20.990
Father?

00:36:45.700 --> 00:36:50.600
A Psycommu runaway... Is it thirsty for blood or something?!

00:36:52.090 --> 00:36:56.100
This is a... This is nothing but a slaughter!

00:36:57.670 --> 00:37:01.970
This doesn't seem like an act of people who see themselves as Char's successors.

00:37:01.970 --> 00:37:02.640
How many?

00:37:02.640 --> 00:37:07.520
There are four small transports and one mid-sized VTOL craft above the area.

00:37:07.520 --> 00:37:12.330
Do you think I'm lucky enough for that to be the camouflaged freighter?

00:37:12.650 --> 00:37:15.190
I've intercepted the enemy's trunk line, sir!

00:37:15.190 --> 00:37:17.330
This is the group that attacked Dakar?

00:37:17.670 --> 00:37:21.340
All hands, level two battle stations! Mobile suits on standby!

00:37:23.030 --> 00:37:25.880
Are these people connected to the Box, too?

00:37:32.670 --> 00:37:35.420
Audrey, I suppose you and I can't escape the curse

00:37:35.420 --> 00:37:37.980
of the families we were born into.

00:37:37.980 --> 00:37:40.170
Is this just more useless struggling?

00:37:40.170 --> 00:37:41.270
<i>Hey, newbie!</i>

00:37:41.270 --> 00:37:44.470
<i>If you ever slow us down,</i> <i>I'll shoot you in the back if I have to.</i>

00:37:44.470 --> 00:37:45.890
<i>Remember that.</i>

00:37:45.890 --> 00:37:48.560
This seems like a fine team. I wish I could have joined.

00:37:48.560 --> 00:37:52.490
<i>You can join whenever you want.</i> <i>Just shoot one of us three in the back.</i>

00:37:52.490 --> 00:37:54.020
<i>I'll keep that in mind.</i>

00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:57.830
Pilots have to fight believing in their orders, even if their bosses are morons.

00:37:57.830 --> 00:38:02.420
We lucked out there. At least we serve under a great C.O.

00:38:03.630 --> 00:38:06.050
The commander of the Gundam Corps...

00:38:06.530 --> 00:38:09.510
Gundam... The key to the Box.

00:38:10.870 --> 00:38:12.720
<i>Finish them all off!</i>

00:39:09.320 --> 00:39:10.740
What are you doing?!

00:39:11.470 --> 00:39:13.100
I'm going out in the Unicorn.

00:39:13.100 --> 00:39:17.440
If I break the La+ Program's seal, there won't be any reason to do this, right?

00:39:17.440 --> 00:39:21.150
You can't. If you go out now, you'll be a sitting duck for those flak guns.

00:39:21.150 --> 00:39:22.880
Wait until we're finished mopping up.

00:39:22.880 --> 00:39:24.610
"Mopping up"?!

00:39:24.610 --> 00:39:27.670
Lots of innocent people are dying down there! Is that all right with you?!

00:39:27.670 --> 00:39:30.340
It's an operation. What I think doesn't enter into it.

00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:36.510
Stay put.

00:39:36.510 --> 00:39:39.500
As I recall, we didn't tie you up and haul you with us.

00:39:39.500 --> 00:39:43.520
If you didn't expect something like this, you have a lack of imagination.

00:39:43.520 --> 00:39:46.730
This is what you do when you seize enemy territory.

00:39:46.730 --> 00:39:50.640
Attacking an unrelated area and crushing fleeing people...

00:39:50.640 --> 00:39:54.660
This isn't war, not even close. This is just an act of vengeance!

00:39:54.660 --> 00:39:58.500
That first time we met at Industrial 7, you didn't shoot me, Captain.

00:39:58.500 --> 00:40:00.980
I know this can't be sitting well with you.

00:40:00.980 --> 00:40:02.480
Please, make them stop.

00:40:02.480 --> 00:40:06.250
If this is your idea of war, why did you take me across the desert?!

00:40:06.250 --> 00:40:08.670
Why did you save Ms. Marida?!

00:40:08.670 --> 00:40:12.760
She doesn't call you Master because she's a cyber-Newtype.

00:40:12.760 --> 00:40:16.160
It's because her heart was saved by you, Captain, just like mine was!

00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:18.080
Shut your mouth!

00:40:19.270 --> 00:40:22.590
I worried about you because you're the key to the Box.

00:40:22.590 --> 00:40:25.840
I only won you over because I thought it would make my job easier.

00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:28.220
You said this isn't war, right?

00:40:28.220 --> 00:40:30.190
Open your eyes and take a good, close look!

00:40:30.640 --> 00:40:32.810
Things like this happen in a war.

00:40:32.810 --> 00:40:34.950
There's no principle, no honor, no dignity.

00:40:35.970 --> 00:40:39.040
Some people kill, others are killed, that's all there is to it.

00:40:39.040 --> 00:40:43.940
And what's wrong with vengeance? Our war hasn't ended yet!

00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:47.320
That's exactly how the Federation soldiers who burned the Zeon town

00:40:47.320 --> 00:40:49.130
rationalized what they did!

00:41:13.890 --> 00:41:15.910
<i>Louise, I'm coming to you!</i>

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:21.490
Even though people are sad, we live our lives trying to escape sadness.

00:41:21.810 --> 00:41:23.580
You told me that!

00:41:25.070 --> 00:41:26.000
You little punk!

00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.790
You know it, too!

00:41:27.790 --> 00:41:31.210
Doing this won't accomplish anything!

00:41:31.210 --> 00:41:34.300
You're just an ignorant little kid!

00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:40.920
I... We have been waiting for this moment for a long, long time.

00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:43.600
So long that I want to get out right now to help out!

00:41:43.600 --> 00:41:47.320
Just because you've seen hell with your own two eyes

00:41:47.320 --> 00:41:50.650
doesn't mean you can force that hell on other-

00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:53.740
If you don't quit your yammering, so help me, I swear I'll-

00:41:58.060 --> 00:42:01.350
Do something about this kid! Alec! Flaste!

00:42:01.350 --> 00:42:05.540
Sorry, my hands are full right now, sir. You'll have to do it yourself.

00:42:05.860 --> 00:42:07.170
You sons of-

00:42:09.690 --> 00:42:13.550
I don't get it... I just don't understand this.

00:42:14.200 --> 00:42:19.290
But it's wrong to close off your heart just because

00:42:19.290 --> 00:42:23.260
there are too many sad and painful things out there.

00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:27.420
I don't want to forget the sadness that people are feeling.

00:42:27.420 --> 00:42:30.920
The fact that we have hearts is why we can feel sadness!

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:33.270
I want to become the sort of man who can live with that!

00:42:34.260 --> 00:42:36.470
The sort of man you are, Captain!

00:43:08.040 --> 00:43:09.090
Banagher?

00:43:09.090 --> 00:43:11.730
<i>Mr. Tomura, please send out</i> <i>the Unicorn Gundam.</i>

00:43:11.730 --> 00:43:13.590
I thought you were on standby.

00:43:36.920 --> 00:43:40.380
<i>Loni, stop it! Leave from the</i> <i>east side and head for the base!</i>

00:43:47.310 --> 00:43:50.790
<i>Are you sure about this? If I drop</i> <i>him now, he'll be a sitting duck!</i>

00:43:56.480 --> 00:44:00.740
<i>It's all right. Let the kid do</i> <i>what he wants. Right, Captain?</i>

00:44:06.270 --> 00:44:09.810
Captain, everyone on the Garencieres, thank you for looking after me.

00:44:10.520 --> 00:44:13.330
Banagher Links in the Unicorn Gundam, here I go!

00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:14.900
Release!

00:44:21.340 --> 00:44:23.840
I'm not the key to some box. I'm a human being.

00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:27.850
And you're a machine that amplifies human abilities.

00:44:28.140 --> 00:44:30.310
That's what you were built for.

00:44:30.310 --> 00:44:34.560
For people who can sense other people's hearts and feel their sadness.

00:44:35.420 --> 00:44:37.820
So don't let anger swallow you up.

00:44:41.050 --> 00:44:43.950
It's the Split-horn? It's too soon, Garencieres!

00:44:43.950 --> 00:44:45.160
What's it-

00:44:56.780 --> 00:44:58.650
Has that boy betrayed us?

00:44:58.650 --> 00:45:01.670
<i>I'm going to break the Box's seal!</i> <i>Fall back, you guys!</i>

00:45:01.670 --> 00:45:03.930
Why is the Box's key getting in the way?!

00:45:16.630 --> 00:45:17.520
<i>Kirks.</i>

00:45:17.980 --> 00:45:19.020
<i>Loni, what is it?</i>

00:45:21.110 --> 00:45:23.680
<i>The Split-horn opened fire on me.</i>

00:45:26.640 --> 00:45:29.120
What do you mean?

00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:33.230
<i>It's time to go, Loni!</i>

00:45:33.230 --> 00:45:35.900
We've taken a long, winding road to get here.

00:45:35.900 --> 00:45:37.500
If anyone stands in our way, I'll crush them!

00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:39.460
I don't like this.

00:45:39.460 --> 00:45:42.570
<i>What is this, a walking war museum?</i>

00:45:42.570 --> 00:45:44.740
<i>They've got guts, attacking in suits like those.</i>

00:45:44.740 --> 00:45:48.720
<i>That's why we can't let our guard down.</i> <i>We don't have tenacity like that.</i>

00:45:53.500 --> 00:45:55.340
<i>Why are you doing this?!</i>

00:45:55.340 --> 00:45:56.940
<i>This is what I've been living for.</i>

00:45:56.940 --> 00:45:58.100
Banagher?!

00:45:58.100 --> 00:46:00.510
I owe you all a debt of gratitude.

00:46:00.510 --> 00:46:02.860
Thanks to the Garencieres crashing in the desert,

00:46:02.860 --> 00:46:05.990
<i>we have the chance to take our</i> <i>revenge after all these years.</i>

00:46:05.990 --> 00:46:11.020
You're too late. If you stop me, this truly will have been for nothing.

00:46:11.020 --> 00:46:14.250
Get out of the way! And hurry up and turn into the Split-horn!

00:46:14.250 --> 00:46:17.730
You can't! The people who were killed here and their families

00:46:17.730 --> 00:46:20.250
will only make your people hated even more!

00:46:27.370 --> 00:46:29.290
You're wasting your time...

00:46:44.220 --> 00:46:45.510
Stop it!

00:46:45.510 --> 00:46:49.950
If this cycle continues, your heart will break and you'll lose your humanity!

00:46:49.950 --> 00:46:54.190
Shut your mouth! My father and mother died in the hunt for Zeon remnants!

00:46:54.190 --> 00:46:57.750
They were killed without being allowed to surrender! Butchered!

00:46:58.160 --> 00:47:02.250
<i>I'm here because I devoted my life</i> <i>to finishing what my father started!</i>

00:47:02.250 --> 00:47:04.030
Your precious Box can stay shut!

00:47:04.030 --> 00:47:07.840
My hatred runs too deep for something like that to dispel it!

00:47:07.840 --> 00:47:09.630
Get out of my way!

00:47:16.250 --> 00:47:17.180
<i>Banagher!</i>

00:47:25.780 --> 00:47:28.470
<i>Ensign Riddhe, if we don't stop</i> <i>that thing, the city will be-</i>

00:47:28.470 --> 00:47:32.660
I know, but nothing we say will change its pilot's mind. We have to destroy it.

00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:35.190
Brute force won't solve anything!

00:47:35.190 --> 00:47:38.440
She's enslaved, that's all! That's not the real her.

00:47:38.440 --> 00:47:39.210
I will stop her!

00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:44.700
You're right, she is enslaved.

00:47:44.700 --> 00:47:46.880
By a blood curse that can never be broken.

00:47:49.590 --> 00:47:51.380
<i>Listen to me, Ms. Loni!</i>

00:47:51.380 --> 00:47:55.680
Is this what you really want? Is this what the real you wants?!

00:47:57.830 --> 00:47:58.680
<i>Ms. Loni!</i>

00:47:59.210 --> 00:48:00.880
But, this is all I have...

00:48:00.880 --> 00:48:05.610
I don't have anything else to live for.

00:48:05.610 --> 00:48:10.090
<i>Then find something! It's too sad to</i> <i>live for nothing but hatred and anger.</i>

00:48:10.090 --> 00:48:14.020
It's only human to be angered by injustice! People aren't gods!

00:48:14.020 --> 00:48:17.080
<i>Even so! You have to stop this!</i>

00:48:26.790 --> 00:48:28.550
Are you crazy, Banagher?!

00:48:39.290 --> 00:48:40.520
It stopped...?

00:48:49.010 --> 00:48:53.140
Father, Mother... I...

00:49:14.160 --> 00:49:16.140
I'll cover you! Fall back!

00:49:20.710 --> 00:49:21.960
Shit!

00:49:38.850 --> 00:49:39.640
<i>Watts!</i>

00:49:39.640 --> 00:49:41.160
<i>I told you not to let your guard down!</i>

00:49:43.730 --> 00:49:45.250
One shot left, huh?

00:49:57.010 --> 00:49:57.760
Bastard!

00:50:03.100 --> 00:50:04.310
Loni...

00:50:04.750 --> 00:50:09.860
You mustn't end up like us!

00:50:24.940 --> 00:50:27.480
They killed Kirks?

00:50:27.480 --> 00:50:31.900
The Federation took away another person who protected me...

00:50:31.900 --> 00:50:33.500
The last of my family!

00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:34.460
Ms. Loni!

00:50:35.320 --> 00:50:39.180
This is the only place for me now!

00:50:50.600 --> 00:50:53.610
You can't fight reality.

00:51:00.100 --> 00:51:05.600
I... I want to stop her. I have to stop her!

00:51:05.600 --> 00:51:06.500
Gundam!

00:51:12.820 --> 00:51:14.780
Give me strength!

00:51:27.390 --> 00:51:29.230
Gundam...

00:51:29.230 --> 00:51:31.000
<i>Lieutenant... That's...</i>

00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:31.730
Yeah.

00:51:43.850 --> 00:51:44.620
Move!

00:52:00.420 --> 00:52:03.010
Banagher, what are you doing?! Shoot her!

00:52:07.520 --> 00:52:10.130
Don't interfere!

00:52:11.340 --> 00:52:15.300
You'll pay! You'll pay! You'll pay!

00:52:17.680 --> 00:52:20.390
<i>This stagnant, black feeling...</i>

00:52:20.390 --> 00:52:23.990
<i>There's no point in becoming stained</i> <i>through and through with it.</i>

00:52:31.500 --> 00:52:33.960
Don't let it consume you, Ms. Loni!

00:52:33.960 --> 00:52:38.660
Children are always consumed by their parents' wishes, Banagher.

00:52:38.660 --> 00:52:40.240
I'm not wrong!

00:52:40.240 --> 00:52:42.840
That's not a wish! It's a curse!

00:52:42.840 --> 00:52:45.750
It's the same thing! You carry out what was entrusted to you!

00:52:45.750 --> 00:52:49.930
That's the duty of the children bound by blood to the parents who gave them life!

00:52:49.930 --> 00:52:54.350
And you're one to talk, your power was given to you by your parents, too!

00:52:59.360 --> 00:53:02.280
This is my war!

00:53:07.320 --> 00:53:08.700
<i>Get on, Banagher!</i>

00:53:12.440 --> 00:53:15.440
We have to exceed the reaction speed of those reflectors.

00:53:15.440 --> 00:53:16.460
How's your beam magnum?

00:53:16.460 --> 00:53:17.940
One shot left.

00:53:17.940 --> 00:53:19.170
<i>It all comes down to one shot, then.</i>

00:53:19.170 --> 00:53:19.950
Mr. Riddhe...

00:53:19.950 --> 00:53:23.800
<i>Do it! It's the only way to protect the city!</i>

00:53:23.800 --> 00:53:26.260
<i>We'll fly around and then charge straight at the chest.</i>

00:53:26.450 --> 00:53:28.960
<i>We'll split up as we pass her, attack simultaneously,</i>

00:53:28.960 --> 00:53:30.960
<i>and break through in one spot!</i>

00:53:32.290 --> 00:53:36.900
Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon...

00:53:40.860 --> 00:53:47.990
<i>Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon...</i>

00:53:56.710 --> 00:53:58.710
Ms. Loni! Come back!

00:53:58.710 --> 00:54:00.710
Give it up, already!

00:54:01.320 --> 00:54:02.700
Sieg Zeon!

00:54:05.160 --> 00:54:08.660
<i>Loni... Our war is over.</i>

00:54:19.420 --> 00:54:20.140
Ms. Loni...

00:54:20.140 --> 00:54:22.440
Banagher, shoot while you can!

00:54:30.450 --> 00:54:33.120
You're risking your life over a possibility!

00:54:34.200 --> 00:54:36.900
Just give up on it and let go!

00:54:39.280 --> 00:54:40.500
<i>Banagher.</i>

00:54:46.320 --> 00:54:47.680
<i>It's sad, isn't it?</i>

00:54:47.680 --> 00:54:49.090
I can't shoot!

00:55:21.230 --> 00:55:24.110
The massive mobile armor has stopped moving.

00:55:24.110 --> 00:55:26.670
The other Zeon Remnant mobile suits seem to have been mopped up.

00:55:27.320 --> 00:55:30.080
Verifying damage to Torrington Base.

00:55:30.080 --> 00:55:33.390
Get me Romeo 008 first.

00:55:34.250 --> 00:55:38.420
Flaste, take us out of this airspace.

00:55:53.560 --> 00:55:55.490
<i>Come down from there, Banagher.</i>

00:55:57.750 --> 00:56:00.570
<i>A seizure order has been issued for that Gundam.</i>

00:56:00.570 --> 00:56:02.120
<i>Step out and hand it over.</i>

00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:05.130
<i>Ensign Riddhe...</i>

00:56:05.780 --> 00:56:10.380
<i>If it weren't for you, none of this</i> <i>would have happened.</i>

00:56:19.630 --> 00:56:20.430
A black...

00:56:22.840 --> 00:56:24.400
Unicorn...?

00:56:33.400 --> 00:56:37.840
<i>ate mo naku ochite yuku hoshi no</i>

00:56:33.400 --> 00:56:37.840
<i>When a star is falling down aimlessly</i>

00:56:37.840 --> 00:56:42.240
<i>kagayaki wa nageki ni nite</i>

00:56:37.840 --> 00:56:42.240
<i>Its radiance resembles grief</i>

00:56:42.240 --> 00:56:46.540
<i>taema naku kanashimi wo daku no</i>

00:56:42.240 --> 00:56:46.540
<i>Ceaselessly embracing sorrow</i>

00:56:46.540 --> 00:56:55.070
<i>sore dake ga shinjitsu nara</i>

00:56:46.540 --> 00:56:55.070
<i>If that is the only truth</i>

00:56:59.760 --> 00:57:04.260
<i>kowareteku keshiki no kakera ni</i>

00:56:59.760 --> 00:57:04.260
<i>On fragments of the disintegrating landscape</i>

00:57:04.260 --> 00:57:08.660
<i>naiteiru kimi ga utsuru yo</i>

00:57:04.260 --> 00:57:08.660
<i>I see the reflection of you in tears</i>

00:57:08.660 --> 00:57:13.010
<i>atatakana kioku no naka de wa</i>

00:57:08.660 --> 00:57:13.010
<i>Reminiscing on the warm memories</i>

00:57:13.010 --> 00:57:25.180
<i>tsuyoku te wo tsunaida mama Ah</i>

00:57:13.010 --> 00:57:25.180
<i>Of when we held our hands tight... Ah</i>

00:57:25.180 --> 00:57:30.130
<i>omoi wa hane wo hirogete rasen wo egaku you ni</i>

00:57:25.180 --> 00:57:30.130
<i>The feelings spread their wings, and as if tracing a spiral,</i>

00:57:30.130 --> 00:57:34.250
<i>bokura no ashita e maiagaru</i>

00:57:30.130 --> 00:57:34.250
<i>They soar into our tomorrow</i>

00:57:34.250 --> 00:57:38.690
<i>Oh, feel my soul hibiku kodou</i>

00:57:34.250 --> 00:57:38.690
<i>Oh, feel my soul, the resonant heartbeat</i>

00:57:38.690 --> 00:57:43.050
<i>onaji kono toki wo ikiteru</i>

00:57:38.690 --> 00:57:43.050
<i>We're living in the same moment</i>

00:57:43.050 --> 00:57:47.780
<i>omoikiri sakebu koe ga kikoenai kyori demo</i>

00:57:43.050 --> 00:57:47.780
<i>Even if we're so far apart that we can't hear each other shouting,</i>

00:57:47.780 --> 00:57:51.890
<i>kitto sono mune ni todoku kara</i>

00:57:47.780 --> 00:57:51.890
<i>I'm sure the voice will reach each other's heart</i>

00:57:51.890 --> 00:57:56.300
<i>Go around and round, there is no end of the world</i>

00:57:56.300 --> 00:58:05.480
<i>onaji yami ni ukabu yume wo miyou</i>

00:57:56.300 --> 00:58:05.480
<i>Let's have a dream surfacing from the same darkness</i>

00:58:19.060 --> 00:58:23.530
<i>yasashisa ja nani mo sukuenai</i>

00:58:19.060 --> 00:58:23.530
<i>Kindness can't save anything</i>

00:58:23.530 --> 00:58:27.990
<i>nomareteku mujun no sekai</i>

00:58:23.530 --> 00:58:27.990
<i>This world of contradictions is being consumed</i>

00:58:27.990 --> 00:58:32.360
<i>moshi kimi to deawanakattara</i>

00:58:27.990 --> 00:58:32.360
<i>If we had not met</i>

00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:44.720
<i>kodoku sae shiranai mama Ah</i>

00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:44.720
<i>I would not even know loneliness... Ah</i>

00:58:44.720 --> 00:58:49.380
<i>negai wa hane wo hirogete towa wo kanaderu you ni</i>

00:58:44.720 --> 00:58:49.380
<i>The wishes spread their wings and, as if playing the tune of eternity,</i>

00:58:49.380 --> 00:58:53.600
<i>kaze no mukou e to kakete yuku</i>

00:58:49.380 --> 00:58:53.600
<i>They fly off beyond the wind</i>

00:58:53.600 --> 00:58:58.000
<i>Oh find the light sono yokogao</i>

00:58:53.600 --> 00:58:58.000
<i>Oh, find the light, the side face,</i>

00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:02.420
<i>kimi to kono sora wo miageru</i>

00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:02.420
<i>I look up at the universe with you</i>

00:59:02.420 --> 00:59:07.070
<i>unmei no uzu no naka de kono te nobashi nagara</i>

00:59:02.420 --> 00:59:07.070
<i>Stretching this hand in the swirl of fate,</i>

00:59:07.070 --> 00:59:11.120
<i>Never come back again, I know I'm in my dream</i>

00:59:11.120 --> 00:59:15.590
<i>namida mo uketomeru kara</i>

00:59:11.120 --> 00:59:15.590
<i>I'll take in your tears</i>

00:59:15.590 --> 00:59:24.990
<i>onaji yami wo terashi daseru hi made</i>

00:59:15.590 --> 00:59:24.990
<i>Until the day they can illuminate the same darkness</i>
